§ `Part 13 Chapter 6 -- Records of resolutions and meetings`

-- ---- s 355 Records of resolutions and meetings etc ---------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 355(1) record` IS ONE OF
    `s 355(1)(a) copies of all resolutions of members passed otherwise than at general meetings`
    `s 355(1)(b) minutes of all proceedings of general meetings`
    `s 355(1)(c) details provided to the company in accordance with section 357 (decisions of sole member)`
    `s 355(1) another record`

-- src:4555 | (1) Every company must keep records comprising—
-- src:4556 | (a) copies of all resolutions of members passed otherwise than at general meetings,
-- src:4557 | (b) minutes of all proceedings of general meetings, and
-- src:4558 | (c) details provided to the company in accordance with section 357 (decisions of sole member).
@ref s 355(1) Records of resolutions and meetings etc (src:4555-4558)
GIVEN record IS A `s 355(1) record`
      `the company has kept the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355(1) the company has kept the record this subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER record
    WHEN `s 355(1) another record` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every company must keep records comprising— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..."
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the company has kept the record`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must keep records comprising—" -- FORK F5

-- "kept for at least ten years from the date": the period of ten years beginning with the date ends the day before the tenth anniversary.
-- src:4559 | (2) The records must be kept for at least ten years from the date of the resolution, meeting or decision (as appropriate).
@ref s 355(2) Records of resolutions and meetings etc: ten years (src:4559)
GIVEN `the date of the resolution, meeting or decision` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the record was kept` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355(2) the record was kept for at least ten years` MEANS
    IF `the last day on which the record was kept` AT LEAST (`add years` `the date of the resolution, meeting or decision` 10) MINUS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The records must be kept for at least ten years from the date of the resolution, meeting or decision (as appropriate)" -- FORK F7

-- src:4560 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 355(3) Records of resolutions and meetings etc: offence (src:4560)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with this section`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4561 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 355(4) Records of resolutions and meetings etc: penalty (src:4561)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 355(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)

-- ---- s 356 Records as evidence of resolutions etc ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4563 | (1) This section applies to the records kept in accordance with section 355.
@ref s 356(1) Records as evidence of resolutions etc: application (src:4563)
GIVEN `the record is kept in accordance with section 355` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356(1) this section applies to the record` MEANS
    IF `the record is kept in accordance with section 355`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to the records kept in accordance with section 355"

-- src:4564 | (2) The record of a resolution passed otherwise than at a general meeting, if purporting to be signed by a director of the company or by the company secretary, is evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the passing of the resolution.
@ref s 356(2) Records as evidence of resolutions etc: resolutions passed otherwise than at a general meeting (src:4564)
GIVEN `the record is of a resolution passed otherwise than at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record purports to be signed by a director of the company or by the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356(2) the record is evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the passing of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the record is of a resolution passed otherwise than at a general meeting` AND `the record purports to be signed by a director of the company or by the company secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The record of a resolution passed otherwise than at a general meeting, if purporting to be signed by a director of the company or by the company secretary, is evidence"

-- src:4565 | (3) Where there is a record of a written resolution of a private company, the requirements of this Act with respect to the passing of the resolution are deemed to be complied with unless the contrary is proved.
@ref s 356(3) Records as evidence of resolutions etc: written resolutions of private companies (src:4565)
GIVEN `there is a record of a written resolution of a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356(3) the requirements of this Act with respect to the passing of the resolution are deemed to be complied with` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there is a record of a written resolution of a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where there is a record of a written resolution of a private company"
    ELSE IF `the contrary is proved`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "deemed to be complied with unless the contrary is proved"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4566 | (4) The minutes of proceedings of a general meeting, if purporting to be signed by the chairman of that meeting or by the chairman of the next general meeting, are evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the proceedings at the meeting.
@ref s 356(4) Records as evidence of resolutions etc: minutes of general meetings (src:4566)
GIVEN `the minutes are of proceedings of a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minutes purport to be signed by the chairman of that meeting or by the chairman of the next general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356(4) the minutes are evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the proceedings at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the minutes are of proceedings of a general meeting` AND `the minutes purport to be signed by the chairman of that meeting or by the chairman of the next general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The minutes of proceedings of a general meeting, if purporting to be signed by the chairman of that meeting or by the chairman of the next general meeting, are evidence"

DECLARE `s 356(5) deemed fact` IS ONE OF
    `s 356(5)(a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened`
    `s 356(5)(b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place`
    `s 356(5)(c) all appointments at the meeting are deemed valid`

-- src:4567 | (5) Where there is a record of proceedings of a general meeting of a company, then, until the contrary is proved—
-- src:4568 | (a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened,
-- src:4569 | (b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place, and
-- src:4570 | (c) all appointments at the meeting are deemed valid.
@ref s 356(5) Records as evidence of resolutions etc: proceedings of a general meeting (src:4567-4570)
GIVEN `there is a record of proceedings of a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      fact IS A `s 356(5) deemed fact`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356(5) the fact is deemed` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there is a record of proceedings of a general meeting of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where there is a record of proceedings of a general meeting of a company"
    ELSE IF `the contrary is proved`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, until the contrary is proved— (a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened, (b) ..., and (c) ..."
         ELSE CONSIDER fact
              WHEN `s 356(5)(a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 356(5)(b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 356(5)(c) all appointments at the meeting are deemed valid` THEN JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 357 Records of decisions by sole member ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4572 | (1) This section applies to a company limited by shares or by guarantee that has only one member.
@ref s 357(1) Records of decisions by sole member: application (src:4572)
GIVEN `the company is limited by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has only one member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357(1) this section applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `the company is limited by shares or by guarantee` AND `the company has only one member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a company limited by shares or by guarantee that has only one member"

-- src:4573 | (2) Where the member takes any decision that—
-- src:4574 | (a) may be taken by the company in general meeting, and
-- src:4575 | (b) has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting,
-- src:4576 | he must (unless that decision is taken by way of a written resolution) provide the company with details of that decision.
@ref s 357(2) Records of decisions by sole member: the duty to provide details (src:4573-4576)
GIVEN `s 357(1) this section applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the decision may be taken by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is taken by way of a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357(2) the member must provide the company with details of the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 357(1) this section applies to the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the decision may be taken by the company in general meeting`) OR (NOT `the decision has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the member takes any decision that— (a) may be taken by the company in general meeting, and (b) has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting" -- MARGINAL a
        ELSE IF `the decision is taken by way of a written resolution`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he must (unless that decision is taken by way of a written resolution) provide the company with details of that decision" -- FORK F18
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a company limited by shares or by guarantee that has only one member"

-- src:4577 | (3) If a person fails to comply with this section he commits an offence.
@ref s 357(3) Records of decisions by sole member: offence (src:4577)
GIVEN `s 357(2) the member must provide the company with details of the decision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the member fails to provide the details` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357(3) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the member fails to provide the details`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person fails to comply with this section he commits an offence" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE `s 357(2) the member must provide the company with details of the decision`

-- src:4578 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 2 on the standard scale.
@ref s 357(4) Records of decisions by sole member: penalty (src:4578)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 357(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 2, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 2, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 2, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 2, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
-- src:4579 | (5) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of any decision referred to in subsection (2).
@ref s 357(5) Records of decisions by sole member: validity (src:4579)
GIVEN `the member failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357(5) the failure affects the validity of any decision referred to in subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the member failed to comply with this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of any decision referred to in subsection (2)."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply

-- ---- s 358 Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings -------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 358(1) place` IS ONE OF
    `s 358(1)(a) the company's registered office`
    `s 358(1)(b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136`
    `s 358(1) some other place`

-- src:4581 | (1) The records referred to in section 355 (records of resolutions etc) relating to the previous ten years must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:4582 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:4583 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 358(1) Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings: where they are kept (src:4581-4583)
GIVEN place IS A `s 358(1) place`
      `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(1) the records relating to the previous ten years are kept available for inspection at a place this subsection allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 358(1)(a) the company's registered office` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 358(1)(b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136` THEN `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136`
    WHEN `s 358(1) some other place` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available for inspection— (a) at the company's registered office, or (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136" -- FORK F5

-- src:4584 | (2) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:4585 | (a) of the place at which the records are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:4586 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:4587 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 358(2) Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings: notice to the registrar (src:4584-4587)
GIVEN `the records have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change` MEANS
    IF `the records have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office" -- FORK F8
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4588 | (3) The records must be open to the inspection of any member of the company without charge.
@ref s 358(3) Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings: members' inspection (src:4588)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(3) the records must be open to the inspection of the person without charge` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The records must be open to the inspection of any member of the company without charge"

-- src:4589 | (4) Any member may require a copy of any of the records on payment of such fee as may be prescribed.
@ref s 358(4) Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings: copies (src:4589)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(4) the member may require a copy of any of the records` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a member of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any member may require a copy of any of the records"
    ELSE IF `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any member may require a copy of any of the records on payment of such fee as may be prescribed" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4590 | (5) If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (2) or an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused, or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 358(5) Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings: offence (src:4590)
GIVEN `the days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(5) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (2)` AT LEAST 14 OR `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused` OR `a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (2) or an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused, or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4591 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 358(6) Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings: penalty (src:4591)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 358(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), FALSE)

-- src:4592 | (7) In a case in which an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent, the court may by order compel an immediate inspection of the records or direct that the copies required be sent to the persons who requested them.
@ref s 358(7) Inspection of records of resolutions and meetings: the court's order (src:4592)
GIVEN `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(7) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection of the records or direct that the copies required be sent` MEANS
    IF `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case in which an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent, the court may by order" -- MARGINAL a

-- ---- s 359 Records of resolutions and meetings of class of members ------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 359 resolutions and meetings of` IS ONE OF
    `s 359(a) holders of a class of shares`
    `s 359(b) a class of members of a company without a share capital`
    `s 359 another group`

-- src:4594 | The provisions of this Chapter apply (with necessary modifications) in relation to resolutions and meetings of—
-- src:4595 | (a) holders of a class of shares, and
-- src:4596 | (b) in the case of a company without a share capital, a class of members,
-- src:4597 | as they apply in relation to resolutions of members generally and to general meetings.
@ref s 359 Records of resolutions and meetings of class of members (src:4594-4597)
GIVEN group IS A `s 359 resolutions and meetings of`
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359 this Chapter applies (with necessary modifications) to the resolutions and meetings` MEANS
    CONSIDER group
    WHEN `s 359(a) holders of a class of shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 359(b) a class of members of a company without a share capital` THEN
        IF `the company has a share capital`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a company without a share capital, a class of members"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 359 another group` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "resolutions and meetings of— (a) holders of a class of shares, and (b) ... a class of members"
